.TH QFW-DASHBOARD 1 "September 2026" "QFw 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-dashboard \- inspect and operate dashboard capabilities from a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-dashboard
.RI [ options ]
.BR status | diagnostics | events
.br
.B qfw-dashboard
.RI [ options ]
.B action
.I action
.RI [ action-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Calls the same typed capabilities used by the QFw Slurm cluster dashboard.
Output is JSON for CI and diagnostics. This command does not render or require
a browser.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --cluster-root " path"
Select the QFw-SLURM-Cluster checkout.
.TP
.BI --state-root " path"
Select retained dashboard operation and event state.
.TP
.BI --identity " name"
Run an action as root, user-a, user-b, or user-c.
.TP
.BI --request-id " id"
Supply an idempotency identifier for an action.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dashboard-enable (8),
.BR qfw-dashboard-service (8)
